vdagent, gtk: vmlab: pictures on the shared clipboard, and files sent to the guest

The qemu-vdagent channel and the GTK window's clipboard carried text alone. A second
clipboard type, QEMU_CLIPBOARD_TYPE_IMAGE (PNG, the agent's VD_AGENT_CLIPBOARD_IMAGE_PNG),
goes both ways: the GTK side offers and takes pictures as GdkPixbufs, encoded to and decoded
from PNG. A message may now be 64 MiB (was 1 MiB, less than a screenshot), on the way in too.
A paste that waits for the guest's data gives up after 5 s, where it waited for ever.

qemu_vdagent_send_file() sends a file to the guest through the agent's file transfer
(VD_AGENT_FILE_XFER_START, _STATUS, _DATA), one file after another, in 64 KiB pieces while
less than 256 KiB is waiting to go out. The agent saves it on the desktop. (The user's request.)

